{
 "name": "seesaw_L2_passive_lowerer",
 "description": "A 62.6 mm tyre four-wheel-drive tractor uses a long, light, freely swinging feeler to lower the raised seesaw before tyre entry. The feeler alone rotates in its round hole on a shaft cross-locked into a two-pin L bracket. Twin booms, mast pin straps, foot pull ties and a twelve-stud motor cradle carry the load. A 12:40 input reduction and two 40-8-40 branches mechanically couple both axles. The only deliberately free loaded mechanism is the roughly 8 g feeler; its two-beam splice has two pins. Timed full-power drive then electrical braking; no sensors.",
